D. Capital management
Regulatory capital
The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) sets and monitors capital adequacy requirements for the Company from time to time.
The Companies regulatory capital consists of the sum of the following elements.
CET 1 Capital includes:
1) Paid up equity share capital;
2) Securities premium;
3) Shares pending for issuance;
4) Special reserve;
5) General reserve;
6) Retained earnings;
7) Other comprehensive income.
CET 1 Capital does not include unrealised fair value gain/loss booked for financial instruments measured at fair value through profit and loss and fair value through other comprehensive income.
Tier I Capital includes:
1) CET 1 capital;
2) Perpetual debt to the extent it does not exceed 15 per cent of its aggregate Tier 1 capital.
The following regulatory adjustments / deductions is made from CET 1 capital:
1) Intangible assets;
2) Deferred revenue expenditure incurred for borrowings;
3) Deferred tax assets;
4) Prepaid expenses;
5) Unamortised loan sourcing cost;
6) Treasury stock;
7) Unrealised gain on financial instruments;
8) Excess interest spread on direct assignment;
9) Average dividend paid in the last three years;

